---
import { SITE } from "../config";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Change this whenever the policy's wording changes.
const updated = new Date("2026-10-21T00:00:00Z");
const updatedLabel = updated.toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
  year: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  day: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
});

const summary = [
  "No account, no sign-up and no login.",
  "Your budgets and usage are stored on your phone, and never sent to us.",
  "No ads, no analytics and no tracking.",
  "Roolio works offline and makes no network requests.",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy · Roolio"
  description="How Roolio handles your data: it's stored on your phone and never sent to us, with no accounts, ads or analytics."
>
  <article class="container">
    <div class="policy">
      <header class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{updatedLabel}</time></p>
      </header>

      <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="short-version">
        <h2 id="short-version">The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          {summary.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="who">
        <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Roolio is an Android app that gives each of your apps a time budget. It's made by {SITE.developer}. In this
          policy, "Roolio", "we" and "us" mean the app and its developer. If you have a question about your privacy, write
          to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="stored">
        <h2 id="stored">What Roolio stores on your phone</h2>
        <p>To do its job, Roolio keeps the following on your device:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The apps you give a budget: their name, package name and icon.</li>
          <li>Each budget's settings: its length, its period, and how much time it can bank and borrow.</li>
          <li>
            How long you used each budgeted app on each day, counted in whole minutes. Roolio doesn't record usage of
            apps without a budget.
          </li>
          <li>Your banked and borrowed time, and the history of past periods.</li>
          <li>Your choices in Roolio, such as whether to stop asking about notifications.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This data lives in Roolio's private storage, which other apps can't read. Roolio also reads the list of apps
          installed on your phone so you can choose which ones to limit, and it doesn't keep a copy of that list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="collected">
        <h2 id="collected">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing. Roolio has no servers and makes no network requests. It contains no analytics, advertising, crash
          reporting or other third-party tracking code. We never see your budgets, your usage or the apps on your phone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="permissions">
        <h2 id="permissions">Permissions, and why Roolio needs them</h2>
        <dl class="permissions">
          <div>
            <dt>Usage Access</dt>
            <dd>
              To measure how long each budgeted app is open. Android shares this with Roolio on your phone only.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Display over other apps</dt>
            <dd>To show the pause screen when an app's time runs out.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Notifications (optional)</dt>
            <dd>
              To warn you 5 minutes and 1 minute before an app is paused, and to show that Roolio is keeping count.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Running in the background and at startup</dt>
            <dd>So Roolio keeps counting while you use other apps, and starts again after your phone restarts.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          You can turn off any of these in your phone's settings at any time. Roolio doesn't use Accessibility, and never
          asks for your location, contacts, files, camera or microphone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="backups">
        <h2 id="backups">Device backups</h2>
        <p>
          If backup is turned on for your phone, Android may include Roolio's data in your phone's backup to your Google
          account, as it does for most apps. That backup is run by Google under the
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>, and it's restored when you set up a
          new phone from it. We can't see or reach it. You can turn backup off in your phone's settings, usually under
          Google or System, then Backup.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="google-play">
        <h2 id="google-play">Google Play</h2>
        <p>
          Roolio is downloaded from Google Play, which Google runs under its own privacy policy. Google Play gives us
          summary numbers such as how many people installed Roolio. If you've chosen to share usage and diagnostics with
          app developers, it also gives us crash reports that don't identify you. We use these only to fix problems
          in Roolio.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="website">
        <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses no cookies, analytics or third-party services, and its fonts are served from the site itself.
          If you choose a light or dark theme, your browser remembers it, and that choice never leaves your browser. Like
          any website, the server that hosts it may briefly keep standard request logs, such as IP addresses, to
          deliver the site and keep it secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sharing">
        <h2 id="sharing">Sharing and selling</h2>
        <p>We don't sell, rent or share your data with anyone. We don't have it to share.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="choices">
        <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Change any budget in Roolio, or delete it to erase its usage and history.</li>
          <li>Take back any permission in your phone's settings. Roolio stops pausing apps until it's granted again.</li>
          <li>Clear Roolio's storage in your phone's settings, or uninstall Roolio, to erase all its data from your phone.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="children">
        <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
        <p>Roolio collects no personal information from anyone, including children.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If Roolio changes how it handles data, we'll update this page and the date at the top before the change takes
          effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or requests about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-section);
  }

  .head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  p,
  ul,
  dl {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
  }

  ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li::marker {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .summary {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background: var(--color-surface-container);
  }

  .summary ul {
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
  }

  .permissions {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
